<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS Q1 NET FROM ORDINARY OPS RISES.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS Q1 NET FROM ORDINARY OPS RISES.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1st qtr 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net from ordinary operations   460    vs 377</p>
<p>    ditto per share (guilders)	 1.32 vs   1.10</p>
<p>    Total net profit		   887    vs 692</p>
<p>    ditto per share (guilders)	 2.55 vs   2.02</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		 16.14 vs  15.63</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected Philips Electronics NV to</p>
<p>report a 1997 first quarter net profit from ordinary operations</p>
<p>of between 300 million and 534 million guilders.</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains		427    vs 315</p>
<p>    Income from operations	   836    vs 690</p>
<p>    Unconsolidated companies  loss  10    vs  84 profit</p>
<p>    Financial charges		  167    vs 226</p>
<p>    Tax				    167    vs  93</p>
<p>NOTE - Philips said the extraordinary gain mainly arose from</p>
<p>the partial flotation of its shareholding in ASM Lithography</p>
<p>in February.</p>
</text>
